  "_known_violation": {
    "reverie-scorecard.csv": "TWO violations of the core-prefix rule, both measured at origin/main 2026-08-07: (1) omits the core column 'stdout_parity'; (2) inserts its extra 'tool_count_parity' at index 14, MID-CORE, rather than after the core. Either alone breaks core-position indexing for this variant. This is also why collect-reverie-compat.rs misaligns when it appends into the 33-column canonical scorecard (its DEFAULT --csv target): the columns disagree in content AND order, not merely in count. Recorded, not blessed. Fixing needs the emitter, currently owned by hermit-w7."
  },
  "_core_prefix_rule": "A variant SHOULD be its core columns in core order, then its extras. That is what lets a reader who knows only the core index every core column correctly in any variant. `core_prefix_safe` records whether each variant actually obeys it; the checker reports a violation rather than silently accepting it."
